    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n4687" root="ثمر" body-key="v">
    
      1 
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">ثَمَرَ</span></b> : see 4, in three places. ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  Also <i>It</i>
(fruit) <i>was,</i> or <i>became, ripe.</i> (T.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b3-  <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">ثَمَرَ لِلْغَنَم</span>
<i>He collected trees</i> (which are called <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">ثَمَر</span>, TA [or
rather <i>shrubs]) for the sheep</i> or <i>goats.</i> (K.) ＝   
    <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer1"> </span>-A2- 
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">ثَمِرَ</span>, aor. 
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">ثَمَرَ</span></b> , (tropical:)  <i>It</i> (a man's wealth) <i>became abundant.</i> (A, TA.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">فُلَانٌ مَجْدُودُ مَا يَثْمَرُ</span> (tropical:)  [<i>Such
a one is fortunate in the abundance of his wealth:</i>
or] <i>such a one possesses wealth.</i> (A, TA.)

